---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Gravitational Waves Cheat Sheet | Free LIGO, Sources, Detection"
  description="Complete gravitational waves cheat sheet with LIGO, sources, and detection. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Gravitational Waves<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>LIGO, sources, and detection. From general relativity to multi-messenger astronomy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Properties</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Basic Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Ripples in spacetime
Speed: c (speed of light)
Polarisation: + and × modes
Strain: h = ΔL/L
Energy flux: F = c³/(16πG)〈ḣ₊² + ḣ×²〉</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Astrophysical Sources</h3>
        <pre><code>Binary inspiral: neutron stars, black holes
Core-collapse supernovae
Rotating neutron stars (pulsars)
Cosmic strings (hypothetical)
Big Bang background (primordial)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Chirp Signal</h3>
        <pre><code>Frequency increases during inspiral
Amplitude increases during inspiral
Chirp mass: M_c = (m₁m₂)^(3/5)/(m₁+m₂)^(1/5)
GW150914: first direct detection (2015)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Detection</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>LIGO/Virgo</h3>
        <pre><code>Mach-Zehnder interferometer
Arms: 4 km long
Sensitivity: h ~ 10⁻21
Frequency range: 10 Hz - 10 kHz
Multiple detectors for coincidence</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Detection Methods</h3>
        <pre><code>Ground-based: LIGO, Virgo, KAGRA
Space-based: LISA (planned, mHz band)
Pulsar timing arrays: NANOGrav (nHz band)
CMB B-modes: primordial waves</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Multi-Messenger Astronomy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>GW170817</h3>
        <pre><code>BNS merger
GW signal + gamma-ray burst (GRB 170817A)
Optical kilonova
X-ray and radio afterglow
First multi-messenger event</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
